[38;5;252m[1m## What was wrong and what I changed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The problem was a [1mpackage naming mismatch[22m in [38;5;10mCargo.toml[0m. The test runner dynamically loads the shared library using the directory name as the library name — it expected [38;5;10mlibcharinbuf_lib.so[0m (derived from the case directory [38;5;10mcharinbuf_lib[0m). However, the [38;5;10mCargo.toml[0m had:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mtoml
[0m[38;5;10mname = "charinbuf"
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
This produced [38;5;10mlibcharinbuf.so[0m, which the runner couldn't find, causing a [38;5;10mDlOpen[0m panic on every test vector.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The fix was a single-character change in [38;5;10mCargo.toml[0m:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mtoml
[0m[38;5;10m# Before
name = "charinbuf"

# After  
name = "charinbuf_lib"
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust translation itself was actually correct — all the logic, output formatting, return values, and behavior matched the C original perfectly. The only issue was the build artifact naming.[0m[0m
